    <amendment date="2026-07-22" by="orchestrator (Path A — push-annotations scope discovery)">
      RE-SCOPED to the SAVE path only. The coverage check found `DocxAnnotationWriter` also byte-authors the
      deployed FR-24 push-annotations surface (text-anchored; can't route through the engine without I-7-forbidden
      text-search) — out of this task's scope. Per §6.5 Path A: (1) route SaveAsync/endpoint through
      `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` + wire the client `triggerSave` op-log send; (2) retire
      `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer` FULLY; (3) move the SAVE path off `DocxAnnotationWriter` (save-path
      comments/annotations now via the engine's Apply*), but DO NOT delete the `DocxAnnotationWriter` class or
      `DocxAnnotation.TargetText` — push-annotations still needs them. DocxAnnotationWriter deletion + the
      push-annotations retire/migrate (owner Path B vs C) is **new task 036** (blocks Success Criterion 7 / 060).
      Interim two-byte-author coexistence is a documented §6.5 Path-A exception. Analysis:
      notes/task-032-pushannotations-scope.md.
    </amendment>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
