  <prompt>
    THE WRITE-PATH CUTOVER (FR-06). Route ALL save/annotation writing through `ComposeShadowPatchEngine`,
    then DELETE the two legacy writers: `DocxAnnotationWriter` (whole class, including its `LocateTarget`
    text-search at :316-369 and the `DocxAnnotation.TargetText` text-anchor contract at :611-654) AND
    `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer`. Update `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs`
    to the operation-log save contract — replacing the text-anchored `DocxAnnotation` payload and the
    `{paraId,text}` `ComposeEditedParagraph` payload with the versioned operation log (task 003). A grep
    MUST show NO remaining call sites of `DocxAnnotationWriter`, `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer`, or
    `DocxAnnotation.TargetText`. This is GATED on task 006 (Phase 0 gate) being green (FR-12 / NFR-08) —
    it is an irreversible hard-replace with no parallel-run A/B, so execute the steps IN ORDER. BEFORE
    deleting, CONFIRM the EDGE-1…4 wisdom was already migrated into the Patch Engine by task 030. If any
    behavior only the old writers had is not covered by the Patch Engine, STOP and escalate (Path-B) —
    do NOT delete-and-hope.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer executing an irreversible save-path cutover: comfortable removing a shared,
    load-bearing write path, inverting an endpoint contract, and proving via grep + seam tests that no
    caller is orphaned. Understands this supersedes the R3 paragraph-diff project decision (Path B).
  </role>

  <goal>
    One byte-author remains: all save/annotation writing routes through `ComposeShadowPatchEngine`; both
    legacy writers and the `DocxAnnotation.TargetText` text-anchor contract are deleted with no remaining
    call sites; `ComposeEndpoints.cs` accepts the operation-log save contract; the Tier-1 NetArchTest and
    the updated seam slice are green; and a save submitting a stale/legacy payload shape returns a
    ProblemDetails, not a 500.
  </goal>

